IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mai-dates`
IMPORT `mai-core`

-- Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld) -- a claim for personal injury from a motor vehicle accident, from the seat of
-- the claimant.
--
-- SEAT: the claimant: the person injured in a motor vehicle accident in Queensland, or the person claiming for them
-- (attorney, guardian, administrator) or, for a fatal injury, for the dead person's dependants or estate. "Is mine a
-- claim? Whom do I claim against? What must I do first, and by when? What must the insurer tell me, and by when? Can I
-- go on if my notice was late or defective? What will the insurer pay before the claim is settled? When can I go to
-- court, and by when should I? What costs follow?" Every question is asked as the claimant would ask it, on facts the
-- claimant can state. The insurer's and the court's decisions are facts the claimant answers from what they have been
-- told. The rules are in mai-core.l4; this module builds their inputs from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs
-- with the same meaning have the same name in every question, so the form can ask them once.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 -- the claimant's questions`

-- A placeholder for a date the question's rule does not read.
`a date not used` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000

DECLARE `Claimant answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, I am a claimant`
    `no: there is no claim for damages for personal injury from a motor vehicle accident`
    `the Act's definition does not settle it for someone in my position`

DECLARE `Conference answer` IS ONE OF
    `I may call the conference at a reasonable time and place I nominate from` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Start now answer` IS ONE OF
    `nothing in the Act stops me starting my court action on this day`
    `not yet: I must first give notice of the claim to the insurer (s 37(1))`
    `no: my notice was not given as required and neither the insurer nor the court has accepted it (s 39(5))`
    `no: the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred (ss 37(3), 39(8))`
    `not yet: there must first be a compulsory conference, unless it is dispensed with (s 51A(1))`
    `not yet: mandatory final offers must first be exchanged (s 51C(1))`
    `not yet: a mandatory final offer is still open; I may start from` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE
    `no: the claim is barred because I did not start within the time limit the court fixed (s 51D(5))`
    `no: the period of limitation has ended and s 57 does not extend it`

§§ `Is mine a claim, and against whom (ss 4, 31, 33)`

@export Is what happened to me, or to the person I act for, a claim for damages under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld), so that I am a claimant?
GIVEN `someone was injured in the incident and someone else may be liable for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person suffered personal injury (bodily injury, mental or nervous shock, or death) in the incident and someone may be legally liable for it
      `the liability is covered by compulsory third-party insurance or the Nominal Defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that liability is covered by Queensland's statutory insurance scheme: compulsory third-party (CTP) insurance for a motor vehicle, or the Nominal Defendant for an uninsured or unidentified vehicle
      `I claim damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are claiming, or intend to claim, damages for the injury
      `my position` IS A `Standing` @desc Who you are: the injured person; a person acting for the injured person (attorney, guardian or administrator); a dependant of an injured person who died of the injury; the personal representative of their estate; or someone else
GIVETH A `Claimant answer`
DECIDE `Am I a claimant` IS
    CONSIDER `is a claimant (s 4)` (`the incident is a motor vehicle accident` `someone was injured in the incident and someone else may be liable for it` `the liability is covered by compulsory third-party insurance or the Nominal Defendant`) `my position` `I claim damages`
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x THEN `yes, I am a claimant` ELSE `no: there is no claim for damages for personal injury from a motor vehicle accident`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Act's definition does not settle it for someone in my position`

@export Which insurer do I make my motor accident injury claim against in Queensland: the vehicle's CTP insurer, a self-insurer, or the Nominal Defendant?
GIVEN `the vehicle can be identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor vehicle that caused the injury has been identified (if proper inquiry and search have failed to identify it, answer no)
      `the vehicle had CTP insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a compulsory third-party (CTP) insurance policy was in force for the vehicle at the time of the accident
      `the CTP insurer can be identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer under that CTP policy has been identified (answer yes if the vehicle had no CTP insurance)
      `the CTP insurer is insolvent and its policies were not transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that CTP insurer has become insolvent without its policies being transferred to another licensed insurer
      `a self-insurer owns the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered owner of the uninsured vehicle is a licensed self-insurer
      `the accident happened outside Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened outside Queensland
      `the vehicle is gratuitously insured under s 23(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is one the Act treats as gratuitously insured under s 23(7) (if you do not know, answer no)
GIVETH AN `Insurer answer`
DECIDE `Whom do I claim against` IS
    `the insurer under ss 31 and 33` `the vehicle can be identified` `the vehicle had CTP insurance` `the CTP insurer can be identified` `the CTP insurer is insolvent and its policies were not transferred` `a self-insurer owns the vehicle` `the accident happened outside Queensland` `the vehicle is gratuitously insured under s 23(7)`

@export Whom do I sue in court for my Queensland motor accident injury: the insured driver or owner together with the insurer, or the insurer alone?
GIVEN `the insured person can be identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person insured under the CTP policy (usually the driver or owner of the vehicle at fault) has been identified
      `the insured person is dead or cannot practicably be served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person has died, or it is impracticable to serve court documents on them
GIVETH A `Defendant answer`
DECIDE `Whom do I sue` IS
    `the s 52 answer` `the insured person can be identified` `the insured person is dead or cannot practicably be served`

§§ `Before the claim: the police and the notice of claim (ss 34, 37, 37AA, 40, 57(3))`

@export Must I make sure the police are told about my motor vehicle accident before I claim, and how?
GIVEN `I propose to make a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you propose to make a claim for damages for the injury (yourself or as a representative)
      `the accident particulars were given to police under the road rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the particulars required by the Transport Operations (Road Use Management) Act 1995 s 93(4) were given to a police officer after the accident
GIVETH A `Police notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the police` IS
    `the s 34 answer` `I propose to make a claim` `the accident particulars were given to police under the road rules`

@export By when must I give the insurer notice of my motor accident injury claim (Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld) s 37), and is it late or barred?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day the motor vehicle accident happened, ISO 8601
      `the vehicle can be identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor vehicle that caused the injury has been identified (answer no if the notice is to go to the Nominal Defendant because it cannot be identified)
      `symptoms were immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether symptoms of the injury were apparent straight away
      `the day symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE @desc If symptoms were not immediately apparent, the day they first appeared, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `I have consulted a lawyer about claiming` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have consulted a lawyer about the possibility of making a claim
      `the day I first consulted a lawyer` IS A DATE @desc The day you first consulted a lawyer about the possibility of making a claim, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `I was a minor or under a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 or under a legal incapacity on the day of the accident (s 40 suspends your obligations while that lasts)
      `the day that minority or incapacity ended` IS A DATE @desc The day you turned 18 or the legal incapacity ended, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `I have given notice of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already given written notice of the claim to the insurer
      `the day I gave notice of the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave that notice, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the answer, usually today, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `By when must I give notice of my claim` IS
    `the s 37 answer` `the facts` `I have given notice of the claim` `the day I gave notice of the claim` `the day asked about`
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS `Notice facts` WITH
            `the day of the accident`                                IS `the day of the accident`
            `the vehicle can be identified`                          IS `the vehicle can be identified`
            `symptoms were immediately apparent`                     IS `symptoms were immediately apparent`
            `the day symptoms first appeared`                        IS `the day symptoms first appeared`
            `a lawyer has been consulted about a possible claim`     IS `I have consulted a lawyer about claiming`
            `the day a lawyer was first consulted`                   IS `the day I first consulted a lawyer`
            `the obligation was suspended by minority or incapacity` IS `I was a minor or under a legal incapacity`
            `the day the minority or incapacity ended`               IS `the day that minority or incapacity ended`

@export In the last 14 days of the limitation period, can I give my notice of claim to the Motor Accident Insurance Commission because I am unsure which insurer to give it to?
GIVEN `the last day of the limitation period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period of limitation for your claim under the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (usually 3 years after the accident, as that Act may extend it), ISO 8601
      `the day I give notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you give, or will give, the notice of claim, ISO 8601
      `I am unsure which insurer to give notice to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you want to give notice but are unsure which insurer it should go to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I give notice to the commission` IF
    `notice may validly be given to the commission (s 57(3))` `the last day of the limitation period` `the day I give notice` `I am unsure which insurer to give notice to`

@export My lawyer did not give me the law practice certificate before my notice of claim and I ended the engagement: must the law practice refund my fees, and by when?
GIVEN `my law practice did not give me the law practice certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice you retained before giving notice failed to give you the law practice certificate s 36A requires
      `because of that I cannot give notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of that failure, you cannot give a complete notice of claim within the s 37(2) period
      `I ended the engagement in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you terminated the law practice's engagement in writing
      `the day I ended the engagement` IS A DATE @desc The day you terminated the engagement, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Refund answer`
DECIDE `Must my law practice refund my fees` IS
    `the s 37AA answer` `my law practice did not give me the law practice certificate` `because of that I cannot give notice in time` `I ended the engagement in writing` `the day I ended the engagement`

§§ `After the notice: what each side must do, and by when (ss 37A, 39, 41, 42, 45, 47, 51)`

@export The insurer asked me for more information about my claim: by when must I give it the additional information form?
GIVEN `the day of the insurer's request` IS A DATE @desc The date of the insurer's request for additional information, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give the additional information form` IS
    `the last day for the additional information form (s 37A(3))` `the day of the insurer's request`

@export Has the insurer responded to my notice of claim in time, or is it now presumed to accept that my notice was properly given?
GIVEN `the day the insurer received my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received your notice of claim, ISO 8601
      `the insurer has responded to my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you written notice saying whether it is satisfied your notice was given as required
      `the day the insurer responded` IS A DATE @desc The day it gave you that response, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the answer, usually today, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Response answer`
DECIDE `Is the insurer taken to accept my notice` IS
    `the s 39 answer` `the day the insurer received my notice` `the insurer has responded to my notice` `the day the insurer responded` `the day asked about`

@export My notice of claim was late or did not comply: can I still go on with my motor accident claim?
GIVEN `the claim is against the Nominal Defendant for an unidentified vehicle and no notice was given within 9 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle could not be identified and you did not give notice to the Nominal Defendant within 9 months after the accident (or after a minority or incapacity ended)
      `my notice was given as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice of claim met every requirement of the Act, including its time
      `the insurer said it is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has told you it is satisfied your notice was given as required, or that you have taken reasonable action to fix it
      `the insurer did not respond within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer failed to respond to your notice within 14 days after receiving it
      `the insurer waived compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has waived compliance with the requirement you did not meet
      `a court allowed me to go on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, on your application, declared you have remedied the noncompliance or authorised you to go on despite it
GIVETH A `Proceed answer`
DECIDE `Can I go on with my claim` IS
    `the s 39(5) answer` `the claim is against the Nominal Defendant for an unidentified vehicle and no notice was given within 9 months` `my notice was given as required` `the insurer said it is satisfied` `the insurer did not respond within 14 days` `the insurer waived compliance` `a court allowed me to go on`

@export By when must the insurer tell me whether it admits or denies liability for my motor accident claim?
GIVEN `my notice was given as required, or the insurer did not respond within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice of claim met every requirement of the Act, or the insurer failed to respond to it within 14 days
      `the day the insurer received my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received your notice of claim, ISO 8601
      `the insurer or a court has since accepted my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your notice did not comply: whether the insurer has since told you it waives compliance or is satisfied you fixed it, or a court has declared it remedied or given leave to go on
      `the day of that acceptance` IS A DATE @desc The day of that waiver, notice of satisfaction or court order, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Liability notice answer`
DECIDE `By when must the insurer say whether it admits liability` IS
    `the s 41 answer` `my notice was given as required, or the insurer did not respond within 14 days` `the day the insurer received my notice` `the insurer or a court has since accepted my notice` `the day of that acceptance`

@export The insurer made me a written offer of settlement: by when must I accept or reject it in writing?
GIVEN `the day I received the offer` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the insurer's written offer (or counter offer) of settlement, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I respond to a settlement offer` IS
    `the last day to respond to an offer (s 41(5))` `the day I received the offer`

@export How much of my private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses must the insurer pay before my claim is settled?
GIVEN `the insurer has admitted liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has admitted liability on your claim (in whole or in part)
      `my expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Your private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses reasonably and appropriately incurred because of the injury, in Australian dollars
      `the contributory negligence the insurer asserts` IS A NUMBER @desc The contributory negligence the insurer says is yours, as a percentage from 0 to 100 (0 if none)
      `my needs arose while in the injury insurance scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment, care and support needs arose while you were a participant in the National Injury Insurance Scheme, Queensland, for a serious personal injury from this accident, or after a payment to you under the National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016 s 44(3)(a)
GIVETH AN `Expenses answer`
DECIDE `How much of my medical expenses must the insurer pay` IS
    `the s 42 answer` `the insurer has admitted liability` `my expenses` `the contributory negligence the insurer asserts` `my needs arose while in the injury insurance scheme`

@export By when must I give the insurer copies of reports and documents, answer its request for information, or tell it about a change in my condition?
GIVEN `what I must do` IS A `Claimant cooperation step` @desc Which step: give copies of reports and documents you hold when you give notice; give copies of ones that come into your possession later; answer the insurer's request for information; or tell the insurer of a significant change in your condition or circumstances
      `the day that started it` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave notice, the day the documents came into your possession, the day you received the request, or the day you became aware of the change, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give the insurer documents or information` IS
    `the last day for the claimant's step (s 45)` `what I must do` `the day that started it`

@export By when must the insurer give me copies of its reports and documents, or the information I asked for about the accident?
GIVEN `the day that started the insurer's step` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer received your notice of claim, the day the reports came into its possession, or the day it received your request, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the insurer give me its reports or information` IS
    `the last day for the insurer's step (s 47)` `the day that started the insurer's step`

@export If the insurer paid for my rehabilitation, how is that cost taken into account in my damages?
GIVEN `my damages before contributory negligence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your damages as assessed before any reduction for contributory negligence, not counting the rehabilitation the insurer paid for, in Australian dollars
      `what the insurer spent on my rehabilitation` IS A NUMBER @desc The total cost to the insurer of the rehabilitation services it provided, in Australian dollars
      `my contributory negligence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of responsibility for the accident found by the court, as a percentage from 0 to 100
      `the insurer gave me its written estimate and statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer, before providing the services, gave you a written estimate of their cost and a statement of how they would likely affect your damages (s 51(4))
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How does rehabilitation affect my damages` IS
    `the damages after s 51(9A)` `my damages before contributory negligence` `what the insurer spent on my rehabilitation` `my contributory negligence` `the insurer gave me its written estimate and statement`

§§ `Compulsory conference, final offers and court (ss 51A-51D, 52, 55F, 57) -- once the claim has not settled`

@export From when can I call the compulsory conference myself, at a reasonable time and place I choose, if the insurer will not agree on one?
GIVEN `the day I gave notice of the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the insurer notice of the claim, ISO 8601
      `the insurer asked for additional information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer required additional information from you (the additional information form)
      `the day I gave the additional information form` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the insurer the completed additional information form, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Conference answer`
DECIDE `From when can I call the compulsory conference` IS
    `I may call the conference at a reasonable time and place I nominate from` (`the day` 1 `days after` (`the relevant date (s 51A(3))` `the day I gave notice of the claim` `the insurer asked for additional information` `the day I gave the additional information form`))

@export By when must I give the insurer my documents, statement, legal representation details and certificate of readiness before the compulsory conference?
GIVEN `the day of the conference` IS A DATE @desc The day the compulsory conference is to be held, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I exchange documents before the conference` IS
    `the last day for the s 51B(5) documents` `the day of the conference`

@export The compulsory conference was dispensed with: by when must the insurer and I exchange mandatory final offers?
GIVEN `the day the conference was dispensed with` IS A DATE @desc The date of the agreement or court order dispensing with the compulsory conference, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must final offers be exchanged` IS
    `the last day to exchange mandatory final offers (s 51C(1)(b))` `the day the conference was dispensed with`

@export By when should I start my court action for damages after the compulsory conference (or after it was dispensed with)?
GIVEN `the conference was dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the compulsory conference was dispensed with by agreement or by the court
      `the day the conference concluded` IS A DATE @desc The day the compulsory conference concluded, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the day I gave notice of the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the insurer notice of the claim, ISO 8601
      `the insurer asked for additional information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer required additional information from you (the additional information form)
      `the day I gave the additional information form` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the insurer the completed additional information form, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the day the conference was dispensed with` IS A DATE @desc The date of the agreement or court order dispensing with the compulsory conference, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `a further period was agreed or fixed by the court within the 60 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 60 days, the insurer and you agreed a further period, or the court on your application fixed one
      `the last day of the further period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that further period, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the court dispensed with mandatory final offers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court dispensed with the obligation to make mandatory final offers
GIVETH A `Start answer`
DECIDE `By when should I start my court action` IS
    `the s 51D answer` `the conference was dispensed with` `the day the conference concluded` `the day I gave notice of the claim` `the insurer asked for additional information` `the day I gave the additional information form` `the day the conference was dispensed with` `a further period was agreed or fixed by the court within the 60 days` `the last day of the further period` `the court dispensed with mandatory final offers`

@export Is my motor accident claim barred because I did not start my court action within the time limit the court fixed?
GIVEN `the court fixed a time limit to start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, on the insurer's application, made an order fixing a time limit within which your action must be started (s 51D(4)(b))
      `the last day the court fixed` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that time limit, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `I have started my court action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have started your court action
      `the day I started my court action` IS A DATE @desc The day you started it, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the answer, usually today, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim barred for not starting in time` IF
    `the claim is barred under s 51D(5)` `the court fixed a time limit to start` `the last day the court fixed` `I have started my court action` `the day I started my court action` `the day asked about`

@export The limitation period for my claim has ended or is about to: can I still bring court proceedings because I gave notice of the claim in time (s 57)?
GIVEN `the last day of the limitation period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period of limitation for your claim under the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (usually 3 years after the accident, as that Act may extend it), ISO 8601
      `I have given notice of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already given written notice of the claim to the insurer
      `the day I gave notice of the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the insurer notice of the claim, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the court allowed a longer period to bring proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has allowed a period longer than 6 months after your notice for bringing proceedings (s 57(2)(b))
      `the day I would start my court action` IS A DATE @desc The day you would bring the proceeding, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Limitation answer`
DECIDE `Can I bring proceedings after the limitation period` IS
    `the s 57 answer` `the last day of the limitation period` `I have given notice of the claim` `the day I gave notice of the claim` `the court allowed a longer period to bring proceedings` `the day I would start my court action`

@export Can I start my court action for damages for my motor accident injury on a given day, or does something in the Act still stand in the way?
GIVEN `I have given notice of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already given written notice of the claim to the insurer
      `the day I gave notice of the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the insurer notice of the claim, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the claim is against the Nominal Defendant for an unidentified vehicle and no notice was given within 9 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle could not be identified and you did not give notice to the Nominal Defendant within 9 months after the accident (or after a minority or incapacity ended)
      `my notice was given as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice of claim met every requirement of the Act, including its time
      `the insurer said it is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has told you it is satisfied your notice was given as required, or that you have taken reasonable action to fix it
      `the insurer did not respond within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer failed to respond to your notice within 14 days after receiving it
      `the insurer waived compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has waived compliance with the requirement you did not meet
      `a court allowed me to go on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, on your application, declared you have remedied the noncompliance or authorised you to go on despite it
      `the compulsory conference has been held or dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the compulsory conference has been held, or dispensed with by agreement or by the court
      `the court dispensed with mandatory final offers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court dispensed with the obligation to make mandatory final offers
      `mandatory final offers have been exchanged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the insurer have exchanged written mandatory final offers
      `the day the mandatory final offers were exchanged` IS A DATE @desc The day the mandatory final offers were exchanged, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the court fixed a time limit to start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, on the insurer's application, made an order fixing a time limit within which your action must be started (s 51D(4)(b))
      `the last day the court fixed` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that time limit, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `the last day of the limitation period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period of limitation for your claim under the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (usually 3 years after the accident, as that Act may extend it), ISO 8601
      `the court allowed a longer period to bring proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has allowed a period longer than 6 months after your notice for bringing proceedings (s 57(2)(b))
      `the day I would start my court action` IS A DATE @desc The day you would bring the proceeding, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Start now answer`
DECIDE `Can I start my court action on this day` IS
    IF NOT `I have given notice of the claim`
    THEN `not yet: I must first give notice of the claim to the insurer (s 37(1))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `may proceed`
         WHEN `the claimant may not proceed: the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred, and it cannot waive nor the court give leave (ss 37(3), 39(8))` THEN `no: the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred (ss 37(3), 39(8))`
         WHEN `the claimant may not proceed further: notice was not given as required, and none of s 39(5)(a) to (c) applies` THEN `no: my notice was not given as required and neither the insurer nor the court has accepted it (s 39(5))`
         WHEN `the claimant may proceed further with the claim` THEN `after the notice`
    WHERE
        `may proceed` MEANS
            `the s 39(5) answer` `the claim is against the Nominal Defendant for an unidentified vehicle and no notice was given within 9 months` `my notice was given as required` `the insurer said it is satisfied` `the insurer did not respond within 14 days` `the insurer waived compliance` `a court allowed me to go on`
        `first day after the offers` MEANS
            `the first day proceedings may be started after the offers (s 51C(6))` `the day the mandatory final offers were exchanged`
        `after the notice` MEANS
            IF NOT `the compulsory conference has been held or dispensed with`
            THEN `not yet: there must first be a compulsory conference, unless it is dispensed with (s 51A(1))`
            ELSE IF (NOT `the court dispensed with mandatory final offers`) AND (NOT `mandatory final offers have been exchanged`)
                 THEN `not yet: mandatory final offers must first be exchanged (s 51C(1))`
                 ELSE IF     (NOT `the court dispensed with mandatory final offers`)
                         AND DATE_SERIAL `the day I would start my court action` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `first day after the offers`
                      THEN `not yet: a mandatory final offer is still open; I may start from` `first day after the offers`
                      ELSE IF `the claim is barred under s 51D(5)` `the court fixed a time limit to start` `the last day the court fixed` FALSE `a date not used` `the day I would start my court action`
                           THEN `no: the claim is barred because I did not start within the time limit the court fixed (s 51D(5))`
                           ELSE CONSIDER `the s 57 answer` `the last day of the limitation period` TRUE `the day I gave notice of the claim` `the court allowed a longer period to bring proceedings` `the day I would start my court action`
                                WHEN `s 57 does not help: notice was not given before the period of limitation ended` THEN `no: the period of limitation has ended and s 57 does not extend it`
                                WHEN `s 57 does not help: the 6 months after notice have ended and the court has allowed no longer period` THEN `no: the period of limitation has ended and s 57 does not extend it`
                                OTHERWISE `nothing in the Act stops me starting my court action on this day`

@export If the court awards me a relatively small amount of damages, who gets costs under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld) s 55F?
GIVEN `the damages awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages the court awarded you, in Australian dollars
      `my mandatory final offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of your mandatory final offer, in Australian dollars
      `the insurer's mandatory final offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the insurer's mandatory final offer, in Australian dollars (0 if it denied liability and offered $nil)
      `the lower offer limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The lower offer limit fixed by the Minister under s 100A at the time, in Australian dollars
      `the upper offer limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The upper offer limit fixed by the Minister under s 100A at the time, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
DECIDE `Who gets costs on a small award` IS
    `the s 55F answer` `the damages awarded` `my mandatory final offer` `the insurer's mandatory final offer` `the lower offer limit` `the upper offer limit`
